From: Neogram Patchset <patches@neogram.invalid>
Subject: debloat/greeting-sticker: no greeting sticker in empty chats

Behind NeoOptions.HIDE_GREETING_STICKER. ChatGreetingsView hides its sticker container and says only that there are no messages yet, without the hint to tap the greeting; a business intro set later by ChatActivity keeps its own text.
---
 TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/Components/ChatGreetingsView.java | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/Components/ChatGreetingsView.java b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/Components/ChatGreetingsView.java
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/Components/ChatGreetingsView.java
+++ b/TMessagesProj/src/main/java/org/telegram/ui/Components/ChatGreetingsView.java
@@ -107,6 +107,7 @@ public class ChatGreetingsView extends LinearLayout implements Theme.Colorable {
         if (preloadedGreetingsSticker == null) {
             preloadedGreetingsSticker = MediaDataController.getInstance(currentAccount).getGreetingsSticker();
         }
+        ru.llacker.neogram.chat.NeoChat.onGreetingsCreated(this);
     }
 
     public void setText(CharSequence title, CharSequence description) {
